{title: Holy, Holy, Holy}
{artist: Reginald Heber / John B. Dykes}
{genre: Hymn}
{flow: Opening}
{key: D}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 8장}
{title_ko: 거룩 거룩 거룩 전능하신 주님}
{score: holy-holy-holy.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! [G]Lord God Al[D]mighty!
Early in the [G]morn[A]ing our [E7]song shall rise to [A]Thee
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy, [G]merciful and [D]mighty!
[G]God in three [D]Per[Bm]sons, [D/A]bless[A]ed [D]Trinity!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! [G]All the saints a[D]dore Thee
Casting down their [G]golden [A]crowns a[E7]round the glassy [A]sea
[D]Cherubim and [Bm]seraphim [G]falling down be[D]fore Thee
[G]Who wast, and [D]art, and [Bm]ever[D/A]more [A]shalt [D]be
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! [G]Though the darkness [D]hide Thee
Though the eye of [G]sinful [A]man Thy [E7]glory may not [A]see
[D]Only Thou art [Bm]holy; [G]there is none be[D]side Thee
[G]Perfect in [D]power, in [Bm]love, [D/A]and [A]puri[D]ty
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy! [G]Lord God Al[D]mighty!
All Thy works shall [G]praise Thy [A]name, in [E7]earth, and sky, and [A]sea
[D]Holy, holy, [Bm]holy; [G]merciful and [D]mighty!
[G]God in three [D]Per[Bm]sons, [D/A]bless[A]ed [D]Trinity!
{end_of_verse}
